course: dictionary
lesson: 8229
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and review is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Reviewing something a few days later helps the memory last» tells you review means looking at something again to remember it.
explain: Now read «Watching gameplay videos or reading reviews is a good way for parents to decide about a game.» Here a review is a report saying what someone thinks of something. Check by swapping in your meaning: a report of what people think makes sense in this sentence.
explain: «An appraisal, or performance review, is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year.» It is a grown-up version of a school report. Same word, different job. Always ask: what meaning fits here?
fact: Review can be a noun (a thing, like a review) or a verb (an action, like to review).
fact: «Review» means a second look at something to check it or to remember it.
fact: «Review» also means a report saying what someone thinks of a book, film, game or meal.
fact: In school, to review means to go over a lesson again. In the UK people say revise.
fact: Critics and review sites give scores, but those are opinions, and your own taste may differ. Some online reviews are fake.
exercise: «Ten minutes of practice every day, then reviewing a lesson a few days later, helps the memory last.» What does reviewing mean here? | Meeting the boss for a yearly talk | *Going over something again to remember it | Writing a report about a book | Turning the pages quickly
exercise: Sam reads «Five stars and a long review of the new game.» What is a review in this sentence? | *A report saying what someone thinks of the game | Tidying up the games shelf | A meeting with a teacher | A lesson you go over again
exercise: «Please review your spellings before the test.» What does review mean? | Meet your boss | Write a film report | *Look over again to check | Tear the paper up
test: An appraisal is also called a performance review. What is an appraisal? | A type of online game | *A meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year | Test with a stopwatch | A quiz for fun
test: «Critics and review sites give scores, but those are opinions.» What should you remember about online reviews? | *Some are fake, and your own taste may differ | Every review is always true | Reviews are only for schools | Scores are facts that never change
exam: Marcus says review is always a noun. Is he right? | *No, review can be a noun or a verb | Yes, but only in school | Yes, review is always a noun | No, review is always a verb
